From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 06:12:36 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_sandbox: Hide the System Config -- /etc as an allowlist
 under the host view

Bug 13 of the operator's list of 2026-11-23: the jail could still see the
system above its project. Asked what should not be visible, the operator
named the system itself, /usr and /etc. The host view already hides the
disks, kernel and identity (0158-0161); /etc was still the host's whole
configuration, 227 entries on this machine.

ai-jail 3.5.0-r5 brings --minimal-etc (fork branch feat/minimal-etc): under
--mask-host, /etc is a tmpfs holding only an allowlist of the host's entries
-- 34 here: accounts (passwd, group), name service and DNS, certificates
(ssl, ca-certificates), time zone, the library loader, the shell's startup,
Gentoo's python-exec, eselect and java-config-2, Claude Code's managed
settings -- remounted read-only. Measured there with real bwrap: git,
Node/Python/curl over HTTPS, cargo, rustc, java, claude --version, bash -lc,
date and id all work with it, as without it.

/usr and /opt stay as they are: the toolchains live there (node, git,
cargo; here /opt/bin/claude, rust-bin and the JDKs), and the host view
already hides /usr/src and the kernel's modules.

Zeo passes it like Hide the Kernel (0161):
- agent_sandbox.minimal_etc, default false in default.json and in code --
  off until it has run in daily use, since a tool that reads another /etc
  file would fail -- and per project, set by the Agent Sandbox page's new
  Hide the System Config switch (disabled, with the same note, while Hide
  the Host is off).
- The probe reads --minimal-etc from ai-jail --help; host_args_for adds it
  after --mask-host, only under mask_host.
- On an ai-jail without the option the start is refused,
  minimal_etc_unsupported, naming the option and the -r5 it needs, rather
  than starting a jail that shows all of /etc while the switch says hidden.
- The setting is part of the launch fingerprint, so changing it asks for a
  restart. The ebuild's ai-jail RDEPEND moves to >=3.5.0-r5.

Tests: agent_sandbox minimal_etc_tests.rs -- the option rides --mask-host
only; it is passed when the project asks; off by default; refused, naming
--minimal-etc, on an ai-jail without it; not passed without the host view.
settings_ui -- the switch follows the project, then the default, and is
disabled while the host is shown. Red: with the option's push and the
refusal disabled, the three behaviour tests fail (the two converse ones pass
either way). agent_sandbox, settings_ui and settings_content: 401/401.
---

